{
  "id": "RAW_79ccabc70a",
  "title": "由内而外的 AI：Airbnb 的幕后重构与客端体验",
  "url": "https://www.latent.space/p/airbnb",
  "date": "2026-10-02 22:04:49",
  "author": "Richard MacManus",
  "siteName": "Latent.Space",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div dir=\"auto\" class=\"body markup\">\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_1ac92b22-c007-487c-b80f-f031f36596db_2560x1440.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>Prior to joining Airbnb as CTO in January, </span><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmad-al-dahle/\">Ahmad Al-Dahle</a><span> was head of generative AI at Meta and led the launch of its open source Llama models over 2023-2025. Now Al-Dahle is in charge of turning Airbnb into an “AI-native company”.</span></p>\n   <p><span>What that means in practice is </span><strong>using AI internally</strong><span> to speed up product development, then using those same capabilities to </span><strong>transform the customer experience</strong><span>. We’re calling this </span><strong>an “inside-out AI” approach </strong><span>and in this article we’ll dig into the details.</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f41a8dc3-28da-4dbb-9c8c-bc893cb1dada_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n     <figcaption class=\"image-caption\">An example of inside-out AI: Airbnb used a custom internal tool called Everest to help accelerate the launch of a new external service. (Diagram by Latent Space)</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>Al-Dahle spoke with Latent Space about Airbnb’s AI transformation. We began by asking him why he made the shift from building frontier models at Meta to </span><strong>deploying them at Airbnb</strong><span>.</span></p>\n   <p><span>“Fundamentally, I like to chase where I believe </span><strong>the hard frontiers live</strong><span>,” he replied, pun perhaps intended. “We kind of knew [at Meta] what the flywheel looks like, we understood how to improve the model capabilities, generation on generation.”</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_50e450f9-640f-4bfc-9b3c-0af6d1c30dfc_1236x850.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n     <figcaption class=\"image-caption\">\n      <em><a href=\"https://x.com/Ahmad_Al_Dahle/status/2011440460821320056\">Al-Dahle’s tweet in January</a><span> on joining Airbnb from Meta</span></em>\n     </figcaption>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>The next challenge, Al-Dahle thinks, is deploying models at scale. At Airbnb, his goals are to “</span><strong>push people to work differently</strong><span>, because these tools are transforming how you work,” and to “</span><strong>take these systems and deploy them in production</strong><span>, in creative ways that actually add value to a core user experience.”</span></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Jumping to prototypes, code is the artifact\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><span>From its launch in 2008, Airbnb has been considered </span><strong>a technology company</strong><span> operating in the hospitality industry. The company went public in 2020 and now has a market capitalization of approximately </span><strong>$93 billion </strong><span>(at time of writing). So it’s a big operation to try and make “AI-native.”</span></p>\n   <p><span>Al-Dahle reeled off a few statistics to show that Airbnb is AI-pilled now: </span><strong>60% of its code is now AI-authored</strong><span>, it has </span><strong>shipped nearly 80% more features and improvements</strong><span> year over year, and </span><strong>pull-request throughput for the average engineer is up about 1.6x</strong><span>.</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_ee64deb7-9d81-44ad-8e75-aeace18bf231_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p>But how exactly has Airbnb done all this?</p>\n   <p><span>Firstly, he said it’s about </span><strong>changing the organizational process for software engineering</strong><span>. Traditionally, you might do product requirements, then design work in Figma, then engineering implementation, and eventually production testing. In the past, these would’ve required handoffs from one team to another. But now, </span><strong>Airbnb has its product, design and engineering teams move directly to working with prototypes</strong><span>.</span></p>\n   <p>“Breaking that time down is actually one of the biggest savings that a lot of traditional software companies have to make the leap to do,” said Al-Dahle. “And so we made that leap and it actually ended up adding a ton of tailwind to our product development process.”</p>\n   <p><span>A byproduct of this change is that </span><strong>teams deal directly with code</strong><span>, rather than dealing with “artifacts” like a product requirements document.</span></p>\n   <p><span>“We moved away from excessive artifact generation to </span><strong>the code being the artifact that we reason upon, and prototypes</strong><span>,” he said.</span></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">AI resolves roughly half of support tickets\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p>Al-Dahle told us that customer support was the first user-facing area that it introduced AI into. He described it as “the hardest problem to deploy,” because “the stakes and the consequences of a mistake are really high.”</p>\n   <p><strong>Roughly half of Airbnb’s support tickets are now resolved purely by AI</strong><span>, said Al-Dahle (this is in line with the company’s </span><a href=\"https://news.airbnb.com/airbnb-q2-2026-financial-results\">Q2 results</a><span>, which put the figure at nearly 45%).</span></p>\n   <p><span>The key to this, he says, is using </span><strong>synthetic data</strong><span> to thoroughly test the system before taking it to production.</span></p>\n   <p><span>“We start with: build a model, build the agent, and begin to </span><strong>generate a battery of synthetic data</strong><span> before you ever go into production.”</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_be1c02ab-913c-4018-9bde-96ea30606a5e_2048x1256.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>He notes that although agents handle about half of customer support queries, they are careful about </span><strong>what requires human assistance</strong><span> — with safety issues, for example.</span></p>\n   <p>“So while we solve 50% of the tickets, we’re actually deliberate about the tickets we don’t choose to solve yet [with agents].”</p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Everest, Airbnb’s AI context graph\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><span>Two </span><a href=\"https://www.airbnb.co.uk/services\">Airbnb Services</a><span> projects you may not be familiar with yet are </span><strong>grocery deliveries and airport pickups </strong><span>(the grocery service has just been </span><a href=\"https://news.airbnb.com/airbnb-expands-groceries-with-instacart-across-us-and-canada\">expanded to more cities</a><span>). Both were launched earlier this year, thanks in part to Airbnb’s inside-out AI approach.</span></p>\n   <p><span>It was an </span><strong>internal organizational context graph called Everest</strong><span> that helped bring these products to market quickly. Al-Dahle said that Everest uses technologies such as LLMs, embeddings and AI-based retrieval to build and query the graph.</span></p>\n   <p>He explained that the grocery delivery and airport pickup services are “kind of similar services — API integrations with partner services [external companies] that integrated onto our platform.”</p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png\" alt=\"\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_f8288bd1-6727-4e33-b777-0d61ac37cbe2_1498x988.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n     <figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Airbnb’s new grocery delivery service</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>The grocery service was built first, and learnings from it were made available in Everest. That enabled the airport pickup team to do its project much more quickly. In its </span><a href=\"https://s26.q4cdn.com/656283129/files/doc_financials/2026/q2/Airbnb-Q2-2026-Earnings-Call-Transcript.pdf\">Q2 earnings report</a><span>, Airbnb states that </span><strong>“groceries took eight months, nine months and airport pickups took about six weeks to develop.”</strong></p>\n   <p>Additionally, using Everest means its developers don’t necessarily need specialist knowledge to work on projects.</p>\n   <p><span>“Because of this context graph that exists across the codebase,” said Al-Dahle,</span><strong> “we’re able to have generalists work across very specialist parts of the code</strong><span>.”</span></p>\n   <p><span>Both of the new services were highlighted by CEO Brian Chesky at Airbnb’s </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bFHdNb74YDo\">2026 Summer Release</a><span> in May.</span></p>\n   <a href=\"https://x.com/bchesky/status/2057178134542512476?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset\"> \n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-12 pc-padding-16 pc-reset bg-primary-j62Gac outline-detail-Yl5oYx pc-borderRadius-md sizing-border-box-LGXObM pressable-lg-bfeQpw font-text-a4IB2X tweet-fWkQfo twitter-embed\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-row pc-gap-12 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset\">\n      <div style=\"--scale:40px;\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-width-40 pc-height-40 pc-justifyContent-center pc-alignItems-center pc-position-relative pc-reset bg-secondary-jBBrtc flex-auto-UL7Y7f outline-detail-Yl5oYx pc-borderRadius-full overflow-hidden-owQvYA sizing-border-box-LGXObM container-TAtrWj\">\n       <div style=\"--scale:40px;\" title=\"User\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-width-40 pc-height-40 pc-justifyContent-center pc-alignItems-center pc-position-relative pc-reset bg-secondary-jBBrtc flex-auto-UL7Y7f outline-detail-Yl5oYx pc-borderRadius-full overflow-hidden-owQvYA sizing-border-box-LGXObM container-TAtrWj\">\n        <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_NmAxoKxo.jpg 1x, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_NmAxoKxo.jpg 2x, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_NmAxoKxo.jpg 3x\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_NmAxoKxo.jpg\" alt=\"X avatar for @bchesky\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_NmAxoKxo.jpg 1x, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_NmAxoKxo.jpg 2x, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_NmAxoKxo.jpg 3x\" draggable=\"false\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"img-OACg1c object-fit-cover-u4ReeV pencraft pc-reset\"></picture>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset flex-grow-hUPOlM\">\n       <span class=\"pencraft pc-reset weight-semibold-LL37we reset-PDs18X\">Brian Chesky</span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-B3TpYa reset-PDs18X\">@bchesky</span>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-reset line-height-20-_MEacI font-text-a4IB2X size-15-gjMpX1 weight-regular-CQHCni reset-PDs18X text-aFN1BV\">Introducing the Airbnb 2026 Summer Release</div>\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-reset bg-black-nycVH5 outline-detail-Yl5oYx pc-borderRadius-sm overflow-hidden-owQvYA container-aGHQ9p\">\n      <img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255___ss-rehost__tw-video-preview-13_2057178043706445824.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"image-c_FmAR\">\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n      <div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-B3TpYa line-height-20-_MEacI font-text-a4IB2X size-13-yQMlsX weight-regular-CQHCni reset-PDs18X\">\n       <span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\">7:14 PM · May 20, 2026</span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\"> · </span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\">782K Views</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-B3TpYa line-height-20-_MEacI font-text-a4IB2X size-13-yQMlsX weight-regular-CQHCni reset-PDs18X\">\n       <span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\">327 Replies</span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\"> · </span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\">172 Reposts</span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\"> · </span><span class=\"pencraft pc-reset reset-PDs18X\">3.51K Likes</span>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div> \n   </a>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Choosing which models to use and customizing open models\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><span>To give more of a sense of Airbnb’s internal AI usage, Al-Dahle described it as </span><strong>a “multi-model company”</strong><span> and says it deploys “a lot of different models” in its production systems.</span></p>\n   <p><span>Airbnb uses a mixture of frontier and open models, but </span><strong>conducts most of its own post-training and reinforcement learning on open models</strong><span>. Al-Dahle said the company deploys at least 10 customized models for production use cases.</span></p>\n   <p><span>It also evaluates models along </span><strong>a Pareto frontier for cost, performance and latency</strong><span>, selecting a different trade-off for each application.</span></p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_9ddbeb0b-9402-4914-b491-02f6e3f6a9e2_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><strong>“We run evals specifically for each use case,”</strong><span> he explained. “So if we’re using a model for search, we have a set of search queries that are sampled from production that we measure against. If we’re doing customer support, we also sample all the production queries that we care most about — including edge cases.”</span></p>\n   <p>“We try to use the right tool for the right job,” he added. For example, coding can tolerate more latency but mistakes are expensive. So they prefer to use the strongest available frontier model for coding tasks.</p>\n   <p><strong>“It makes sense to use the absolute most frontier coding model</strong><span>, because for every defect that a model produces, it could easily cost us a lot more.”</span></p>\n   <p><span>On the other hand, search is used at scale by Airbnb’s users and so is very latency-sensitive. </span><strong>So for that job, they prefer smaller specialized models.</strong><span> Al-Dahle claimed that smaller, post-trained models sometimes out-perform frontier models.</span></p>\n   <p><span>“For narrow use cases, we’ve been able to take really small, really nimble models that are very fast and cheap and </span><strong>post-train them beyond the frontier.”</strong></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Async agents: the next big shift\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><strong><a href=\"https://www.latent.space/p/lovable-future-of-saas\">Like other AI-native companies</a></strong><span>, Airbnb has created </span><strong>an internal agent</strong><span> — in its case called </span><strong>AirChat</strong><span>.</span></p>\n   <p>“We have our own internal agent that we call AirChat, which [includes] basically all the necessary MCP organizational context,” said Al-Dahle.</p>\n   <p><span>But Airbnb is also starting to implement what Al-Dahle sees as the next development in agents: </span><strong>asynchronous agents running in containers and activated by events.</strong></p>\n   <p><span>“A lot of our teams are starting to basically automate their on-calls,” he explained. “So if something trips, if a Grafana limit or whatever monitoring system that you use trips, </span><strong>agents spin up to then triage and run your on-call</strong><span>, your initial on-call.”</span></p>\n   <p>A human engineer can review a PR proposed by the agent, while the agent may close the incident itself if it determines that the alert was flaky.</p>\n   <div class=\"captioned-image-container\">\n    <figure>\n     <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"> \n      <div class=\"image2-inset\">\n       <picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 424w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142255_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 848w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 1272w, https://media.bestblogs.dev/20261002142254_996d4acc-4b70-42bd-aa50-1c912c9ee9da_2048x1152.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture>\n       <div class=\"image-link-expand\">\n        <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\">\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"></button>\n         <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\">\n          <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\">\n           <polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line>\n          </svg>\n         </button>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div> \n     </a>\n    </figure>\n   </div>\n   <p><span>This process reminds us of how open source projects like Vercel’s AI SDK, Astro, Flue and tldraw </span><strong><a href=\"https://www.latent.space/p/pr-not-welcome\">use software factories — teams of agents — to apply fixes and features</a><span>.</span></strong></p>\n   <p>Al-Dahle sees this approach eventually being used across its entire marketplace platform; for example to monitor fraud, “trust violations,” marketplace quality, and software defects.</p>\n   <p><span>“My vision is </span><strong>large amounts of asynchronous agents that are helping automate and manage the marketplace.”</strong></p>\n   <h2 class=\"header-anchor-post\">Maintaining the craft of software engineering\n    <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent\">\n     <div class=\"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA\">\n      <button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Link\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft iconButton-mq_Et5 iconButtonBase-dJGHgN buttonBase-GK1x3M buttonStyle-r7yGCK size_sm-G3LciD priority_secondary-S63h9o\">\n       <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-link\">\n        <path d=\"M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71\"></path><path d=\"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71\"></path>\n       </svg>\n      </button>\n     </div>\n    </div></h2>\n   <p><span>Al-Dahle believes that </span><strong>organizing teams around outcomes rather than features</strong><span> is key to becoming an AI-native company.</span></p>\n   <p><span>“If you’re a company that organizes by feature development, you’re going to struggle in the age of AI,” he said. “If you’re a company that </span><strong>organizes by objectives and missions and results that you’re trying to achieve, you’re going to be fine.”</strong></p>\n   <p><span>That said, there’s one thing Al-Dahle worries about during this AI-native transition: </span><strong>whether junior engineers are developing their craft and judgement</strong><span>, given that AI is able to do so much work for them now.</span></p>\n   <p>Senior engineers, he says, have acquired their judgement through many years of shipping systems and operating software in production — including the mistakes they made along the way.</p>\n   <p><span>Part of the solution, Al-Dahle says, is </span><strong>ensuring all of their engineers can explain the work AI does for them.</strong></p>\n   <p><span>“One of the things I’m pushing very strongly is that every engineer must be able to explain, even if an AI generated the PR, must be able to explain what they built. I think if that fundamental premise remains true, then more junior engineers will learn the craft of interface design and architecture, and the importance of testing and unit testing and integration tests. </span><strong>So we’re trying to keep our craft really high.”</strong></p>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Airbnb CTO Ahmad Al-Dahle 解释了“由内而外”的 AI 策略：先利用内部 AI 工具加速产品开发，随后将这些能力扩展到改造客端体验。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Airbnb CTO Ahmad Al-Dahle 解释了“由内而外”的 AI 策略：先利用内部 AI 工具加速产品开发，随后将这些能力扩展到改造客端体验。",
  "summary": "Airbnb CTO Ahmad Al-Dahle 详细介绍了了公司如何通过“由内而外”的方法向“AI 原生”组织转型。该策略涉及在内部使用 AI 来彻底改变软件工程——例如从依赖文档的工作流转向直接进行代码原型设计——这导致 60% 的代码由 AI 编写，功能交付速度提升了 80%。文章还涵盖了内部上下文图“Everest”的使用（该图用于加速杂货配送等新服务），以及一种平衡了前沿模型与基于成本、延迟和性能需求的定制开源模型的多模型策略。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "“由内而外”的 AI 策略",
      "explanation": "Airbnb 优先考虑在内部使用 AI 来加速开发周期，利用这些验证过的能力来增强面向客户的功能。"
    },
    {
      "point": "从产物转向代码",
      "explanation": "通过消除产品需求与设计文档之间的传统交接，团队现在直接与原型和代码进行工作，显著提高了拉请求的吞吐量和速度。"
    },
    {
      "point": "Everest AI 上文图",
      "explanation": "使用 LLM 和嵌入技术的自定义内部知识图允许通用型开发者快速构建复杂的专家服务（如杂货），将开发时间从几个月缩短到几周。"
    },
    {
      "point": "多模型策略",
      "explanation": "Airbnb 部署了至少 10 个定制模型，将昂贵的前沿模型用于编码等高风险任务，并使用较小的、经过训练的开源模型用于搜索等延迟敏感的任务。"
    },
    {
      "point": "异步智能体的兴起",
      "explanation": "下一个前沿是运行在容器中的智能体，由特定事件（如监控告警）触发，以自动化初始的轮班分拣和事件管理。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "我们将这种方法称为‘由内而外’的方法。",
    "其 60% 的代码现在是由 AI 编写的……我们不再进行过度的产物生成，转而让代码作为我们推理的产物。",
    "使用最前沿的编码模型是有意义的，因为模型产生的每一个缺陷都可能轻易让我们付出巨大代价。",
    "我的愿景是大量的异步智能体，它们将帮助自动化并管理自身。"
  ],
